      "en": "Uniterm Indexing was devised in 1953 by Mortimer Taube and represents the earliest successful Post-Coordinate Indexing system. Single concept terms (Uniterms) are assigned to cards with 10 columns (numbered 0-9 for terminal digit filing), and coordination between terms occurs at the time of retrieval by the searcher."
