      "en": "The landmark 'Guide to Reference Books' published by ALA is famously associated with Constance M. Winchell (as well as Isadore Gilbert Mudge and Alice Bertha Kroeger). In the UK, A. J. Walford created the equivalent 'Guide to Reference Material'. Both are premier examples of Tertiary Sources."
