      "en": "A Secret Page (or Key Page) is a predetermined arbitrary page number (e.g. page 21, 51, or 99) designated internally by a library. The library property stamp is embossed on this hidden page so that if the main title page is torn out by a thief, ownership can still be indisputably established."
