      "en": "Weeding out is the direct operational mandate of the Fifth Law of Library Science ('Library is a growing organism'). Just as a biological organism continually sheds dead cells to sustain vitality, a library must discard outdated and physically ruined books to liberate space and keep its active collection vibrant."
