      "en": "As Dr. S. R. Ranganathan famously proclaimed, 'A misplaced book is virtually a lost book'. To prevent books from vanishing due to user or shelving error, library attendants systematically inspect shelf sequences daily/weekly in a corrective routine termed 'Shelf Rectification' (or Shelf Reading)."
