      "en": "PPBS (Planning Programming Budgeting System) was formulated by the RAND Corporation and introduced into the US Department of Defense in 1961 by Secretary of Defense Robert McNamara. It harmonizes long-range goals with distinct operational programs through systematic Cost-Benefit and Cost-Effectiveness analyses."
