      "en": "International archival standards dictate maintaining library storage environments at 20°C to 24°C with a Relative Humidity (RH) between 45% and 55%. Relative humidity exceeding 65% triggers catastrophic fungal/mold outbreak, while humidity dropping below 40% desiccates cellulose fibers, making paper brittle."
