      "en": "Silverfish (Lepisma saccharina) is a major biological pest of libraries. Nocturnal and wingless with glistening silvery scales, it thrives in warm humid darkness, feasting on starch paste, book adhesives, sizing, and paper surfaces, causing surface thinning and irregular holes."
