      "en": "Chemical degradation of machine-made paper stems from inherent acid hydrolysis triggered by alum-rosin sizing and unpurified lignin in groundwood pulp. This generates acid that breaks down cellulose polymer chains, causing characteristic yellowing and catastrophic embrittlement."
