      "en": "Developed by William J. Barrow, Barrow's Lamination process sandwiches deacidified brittle documents between sheets of tissue paper and cellulose acetate film under controlled heat and pressure, reinforcing mechanical tensile strength and rendering the document permanently legible and durable."
