      "en": "Passive RFID tags contain no onboard power source. When interrogated, the tag's antenna captures electromagnetic energy radiated by the reader's 13.56 MHz RF field via inductive coupling. This minuscule induced voltage powers the microchip to modulate and backscatter its identification payload."
