      "en": "A standard PRECIS index entry is formatted into a two-line, three-part layout: the top line contains the Lead (filing term) on the left and the Qualifier (contextualizing terms) on the right; the lower indented line holds the Display (terms subordinate to or dependent upon the lead)."
